  "body": "The remaining public policy/support pages failed contrast and enlarged-text checks. Four legacy pages used 3.32:1 blue links on white (2.92:1 in the deletion badge) and relied on color to identify inline links. At 200% text, long content and the mobile support header overflowed narrow screens.\n\nThis changes only styling: darker blue, persistent link underlines and visible keyboard focus on the legacy pages; wrapping and a stacked phone header keep all nine pages readable. Policy wording, addresses and endpoints are unchanged.\n\nValidation: 54 browser cases across Chromium, Firefox and WebKit at 320/1280px now have zero applicable axe violations, page errors or overflow at normal/200% text. The baseline reproduced 24 failing contrast/link-indicator cases. Chromium/Firefox Tab focus passed; WebKit's default Tab preference skips links, so full keyboard/screen-reader verification is not claimed. The production build passed and all five changed static files are byte-identical to their built output. Initial JS stays within budget (365648 gzip bytes, five preloads). Before/after receipts and images are in the existing audit, finding UX-260917-038; nine existing coverage rows were updated. An initial local static server's incorrect CSS MIME observation was discarded and rechecked with correct MIME.\n\nPrimary WCAG guidance consulted on 2026-09-18 is linked in the audit. No authentication/concurrency behavior changed, so no new model is claimed. Normal merge after independent approval and required checks; verify Cloudflare's resulting static bytes before marking deployed.\n",
